llion and entering the fall with $3.6 million banked. Most race raters call the contest Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Democratic odds near 87 percent.\n\nThe polling picture is thinner than the money gap suggests. The only public survey, an August poll of likely voters, showed Landsman ahead by four points, and its pollster described the race as up for grabs. Conroy has drawn modest outside support while Landsman has attracted almost none, and local coverage has centered on data centers and rising costs. Landsman enters the final stretch favored, but not safely so.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8451, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8473, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8639, "margin": 6.8}]}